{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The digital caliper fits my electronics projects because I could use it to measure components and check clearances before mounting them.",
    "Practical tools connect with my history of buying prototyping supplies, fasteners and a thermometer, though only the caliper meets a clear enough need for me now."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Filament and printer accessories require a printer and a printing project, neither of which is established by my electronics purchases.",
    "The nuts and M6 bolts could help with mounting work, but I would need to know the required thread sizes and lengths before choosing them.",
    "The feeler gauge measures gaps, but I have no current task that calls for that specific measurement."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in electronics projects seems to have been stretched into an assumption that I also use a 3D printer.",
    "Items that belong in a workshop seem to have been treated as interchangeable, even though each needs a specific purpose or compatible device."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My breadboards, PCB supplies, battery holder and relay suggest component assembly and testing more directly than printer maintenance or filament use.",
    "I choose supplies when they serve a concrete task; possible usefulness alone is not enough for me to buy specialized hardware.",
    "The caliper supports several plausible measuring tasks, while the other tools and parts depend on needs I have not shown."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "You recognized my practical project interests, but assumed a specific 3D-printing need that my history does not establish."
}"}
